  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Fish for Development Programme Colombia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will provide technical assistance from the Norwegian Institutions (the Institute of Marine Research (IMR), the Directorate of Fisheries (DoF), the Norwegian Veterinary Institute (NVI) and the Norwegian Food Safety Authority (NFSA) to the Colombian Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Development, Colombian National Authority for Aquaculture and Fisheries, and Colombian Agriculture Institute.  

The Project has two phases, Phase I and Phase II. Phase I will consist of an inception phase with the main objective to finalize a 5 year cooperation programme within fisheries and aquaculture  for the Institutional Cooperation under the Fish for Development Programme in Colombia. Phase II will commence after approval of the Project Document and will consist of implementing the project as defined in the Project Document. The Parties expect the Project to be implemented between 31 October 2021 and 31 August 2027. 
The expected effect(s) on society is improved sustainable socio-economic development for the Colombian fisheries and aquaculture sectors (Impact).</narrative>
  </description>
